postmortems anchored to evidence, with trigger vs root cause, duration gaps and open questions.",[64,65,66,67,10],"postmortem","incident","outage","sre",{"slug":69,"kind":4,"description":70,"keywords":71},"pr","Opens a pull request with a short body that says why, following strict writing rules: no test plan, no file lists, no dashes.",[72,26,44,73],"git","writing",{"slug":75,"kind":4,"description":76,"keywords":77},"pr-address-comments","Pulls review comments on your PR, fixes what is actionable, and pushes, without ever writing to GitHub.",[26,44,78,16],"review",{"slug":80,"kind":4,"description":81,"keywords":82},"release-version-bump","Cut a release for one project in a monorepo: sync, bump only if needed, tag with the CI tag prefix, push.",[83,84,85,86,56],"release","version","tag","monorepo",{"slug":88,"kind":4,"description":89,"keywords":90},"review-pr","Reviews someone else's pull request end to end and writes the review as a local draft file, never posted.",[26,44,17,78],{"slug":92,"kind":4,"description":93,"keywords":94},"start","Pulls the default branch, cuts a named branch from your task description, and starts working on the task.",[72,95,49],"branch",{"slug":97,"kind":4,"description":98,"keywords":99},"test-feature-locally","Verify a change end to end before a PR: bring up compose, start the dev server, drive the touched flow with Playwright.",[100,101,102,103,104],"testing","playwright","docker","e2e","local",{"slug":106,"kind":107,"description":108,"keywords":109},"format-on-edit","hook","Formats and lints each file Claude writes or edits with the tools the project already has.",[34,110,111,112,113],"format","lint","prettier","eslint",{"slug":115,"kind":107,"description":116,"keywords":117},"guard","Denies merges, closes, secret reads, container teardown and shell rewrites of tracked files until you give the go.",[34,118,119,72,120],"safety","secrets","guardrails",{"slug":122,"kind":107,"description":123,"keywords":124},"pre-ship-gate","Refuses commits and PRs that mix moves with logic, add dependencies, skip tests or are too big to review.",[34,72,44,78,125],"size",{"slug":127,"kind":107,"description":128,"keywords":129},"review-chain","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[34,78,44,49],{"slug":131,"kind":107,"description":132,"keywords":133},"stop-check","Blocks the end of a turn while a changed JS/TS project fails its typecheck or related tests.",[34,134,135,136,137],"typecheck","tests","javascript","typescript",{"slug":139,"kind":107,"description":140,"keywords":141},"text-lint","Refuses PR, issue and commit text with dashes, test plan sections, tables, hard wraps or features framed as fixes.",[34,73,44,142,111],"commit",{"slug":144,"kind":107,"description":145,"keywords":146},"worktree-guard","Refuses edits in the main checkout while another Claude session works there, and points you to a worktree.",[34,72,50,51,147],"sessions",{"slug":149,"kind":150,"description":151,"keywords":152},"context-hud","mod","Context window and plan usage limits at a glance: footer gauges, a per-category pane, and a warning past a threshold",[153,154,155,156,157],"context","tokens","usage","limits","hud",{"slug":159,"kind":150,"description":160,"keywords":161},"context-meter","Shows context size and session cost in the status line, and warns once when the context passes a threshold",[153,154,162,163],"cost","status",{"slug":165,"kind":150,"description":166,"keywords":167},"gh-guard","Blocks Claude from posting GitHub comments or reviews as you until you give an explicit go",[26,115,16,78,118],{"slug":169,"kind":150,"description":170,"keywords":171},"read-guard","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[172,153,154,115],"read",{"slug":174,"kind":150,"description":175,"keywords":176},"secret-redactor","Swaps secrets, emails and IPs in tool output and prompts for stable placeholders, and restores real values in tool inputs",[58,119,177,178,179],"redaction","pii","privacy",{"slug":181,"kind":150,"description":182,"keywords":183},"smart-typecheck","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[134,137,111,56,86]],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"item":1,"related":29},{"slug":2,"kind":3,"description":4,"keywords":5,"version":11,"html":12,"skills":13,"hooks":14,"files":15,"sources":22},"smart-typecheck","mod","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[6,7,8,9,10],"typecheck","typescript","lint","npm","monorepo","1.0.0","\u003Ch2>What it does\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>After a turn where Claude edited code, runs \u003Ccode>npm run check\u003C/code> once in each package it touched, and toasts if it fails. You find a type error at the end of the turn, not in CI.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>When to use it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Your packages have a \u003Ccode>check\u003C/code> script (\u003Ccode>tsc --noEmit\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>svelte-check\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>vue-tsc\u003C/code>, a lint pass).\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>You work in a monorepo and only want the packages you changed checked.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>How it works\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Records every successful \u003Ccode>Edit\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>Write\u003C/code> to a \u003Ccode>.ts\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>.tsx\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>.js\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>.jsx\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>.mjs\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>.cjs\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>.svelte\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>.vue\u003C/code> file.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>When the main turn ends, walks up from each file to its nearest \u003Ccode>package.json\u003C/code> inside the session root. If that package has the script, it is checked once, however many of its files changed.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Shows the package name in the status line while the check runs (up to 3 minutes), and a toast if it exits non-zero.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Subagent turns are skipped. Packages without the script are skipped.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Configuration\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Set these with \u003Ccode>/config\u003C/code>, or under \u003Ccode>pluginConfigs\u003C/code> in your user settings.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>script\u003C/code> (default \u003Ccode>check\u003C/code>): the \u003Ccode>package.json\u003C/code> script to run.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>packageManager\u003C/code> (default \u003Ccode>npm\u003C/code>): the command that runs it, as in \u003Ccode>&lt;packageManager&gt; run &lt;script&gt;\u003C/code>. Use \u003Ccode>pnpm\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>yarn\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>bun\u003C/code> if that is what your repo uses.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Requirements\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Claude Code 2.1.287 or later.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>The package manager you configure, on your \u003Ccode>PATH\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[],[],[16,17,18,19,20,21],".claude-plugin/plugin.json","README.md","hooks/hooks.json","hooks/register.test.ts","hooks/register.ts","tsconfig.json",[23,25,27],{"path":18,"html":24},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"modules\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"./register.ts\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">] }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>",{"path":20,"html":26},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Cco